{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790005435,"nonce":"28MPaGPLeddcNm0hH44Zq1DKpto=","title":"dev:debug-action - run any dev-menu entry by label path","message":"Adds a generic route to every mod dev-menu tooling. Filed while testing the Languages mod (rimworld/languages), whose checks (set a pawn language tier, explain mode, round-trip test, comprehension matrix) all live in its [DebugAction] menu and had no bench route.\n\n**Contract**\n\ndev:debug-action {path[], category?, pawn?, list?}\n\n- With no path: lists categories (or, with category, the entries in it).\n- path walks the Actions tree by label, as DebugTabMenu_Actions.InitActions builds it. Matching is case-insensitive and tolerates the T: prefix and trailing ... the menu adds. An unknown or ambiguous label is refused with the candidate labels.\n- A submenu leaf is refused (or listed, with list:true).\n- Action runs action(). ToolMapForPawns runs pawnAction(pawn) with the pawn arg standing in for the click. ToolMap and ToolWorld are refused: their action reads the mouse cell itself.\n- The tree is rebuilt per call, because TrySetupChildren caches a submenu list on the node for good.\n- Output: Log.Message/Warning/Error and Messages.Message text is captured by prefixes for the duration of the call, so it survives Verse.Log having stopped forwarding at its 10000-message cap.\n- Journalled as a dev cheat (Dev.Emit / Dev.Stamp). Result reports windows the action opened, and any exception it threw.\n\n**Acceptance**\n\n1. No path lists categories; category Languages lists its entries.\n2. path [Toggle explain mode] with category Languages runs and returns its message in output.\n3. path [Dump language card] with pawn runs pawnAction and returns the card text.\n4. A submenu path such as [Set language tier..., \u003clanguage\u003e, 2 conversational] with pawn walks the lazily built children and sets the tier.\n5. A ToolMap entry is refused with the reason.\n6. Output still arrives after the log cap has been reached.","files":null}]}